{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1239957-interest-recruitment-for-mage-20-pbp","id":1239957,"title":"Interest/recruitment for Mage 20 PBP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-29T02:55:48-07:00","id":1239957,"title":"Interest/recruitment for Mage 20 PBP","content":"I have collected and read mage the ascension books since the 90s but never found a group I could convince to play it (other than a breif PBP that never really took off because the ST vanished). Recently I have been looking through the aniversary edition and feeling a familiar itch, so I thought it might be time to look for an online game.<br /> <br /> TBH the thought of Story telling mage is a bit daunting as I usually play FATE these days, however realistically I can see that finding somebody else willing to run the game is a long shot so unless anybody wants to step in, I am willing to take it on.<br /> <br /> So I am looking for 3-4 players (actually I would be willing to start out with up to 6, to cover the inevitable attrition with play by post games, but I would be reluctant to start with less than 3).<br /> <br /> Coming from a Fate background (and to reduce the daunting task of settng up a game as open as mage is) I plan on making setting creation collaborative. I will throw in plenty of secrets, but I expect you to take an active interest in the setting, and we will take some time to develop it before launching into play.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, if you are interested I dont want a character pitch. Our first job is to establish the sort of game we want to play and make sure we are all setting out with the same expectations, so to get us started let me know your preferences in terms of:<br /> <br /> Genre (high fantasy? Gritty urban? Dark adventure? Magical espionage? War stories? other?)<br /> Scale (local problems? world spanning conspiracies?)<br /> Focus (at least 2 things you really want to see. optionally, two things you really dont want to see).<br /> Anything else you think is important about the kind of mage game you want to play.<br /> <br /> For my part I am drawn to mage because I enjoy stories about magic, so I would prefer a tradition focussed game to a technocracy focussed game (although I am happy to include technocracy as antagonists - I just want the main focus to be weilders of magic).<br /> Because I find it hard to imagine mages fitting into the standard city based model favoured by awakening and other splats(unless they are a small cabal with few resources), I envision the story to revolve around a chantry rather than a sleeping city. The scale and resources of that chantry may vary depending on the kind of game we decide to run, and depending on what decisions we make it might occupy a very defined space in the world, or may have portals stretching across the globe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T23:44:14-07:00","id":1242630,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd love to play an Orphans game. Very punk and personal, with lots of self discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T03:41:33-07:00","id":1242673,"title":"","content":"I'd enjoy playing in a Traditions game, although I think I'd enjoy a game where other Traditions mages are sometimes just as big an obstacle as the Technocracy. As far as scale goes, I think I'd enjoy the focus on the local. Maybe we occasionally have effects beyond that, but those would be the exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> As far as focus, I'd definitely like to see how mundane and mage life intersects. The weird things you can do with the magic system are cool, but I like to see them given context alongside mundane life. I also like to see everyone starting out as newly minted mages. I like the idea of playing a character trying to establish themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T11:06:06-07:00","id":1243252,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly interested. Wether Orphans, Traditions or Technocracy is not of prime interest to me (I can come up with interesting concepts for all of those), but my favourite part about mage is the paradigm (or in M20 terms the Focus, I guess). I'd love to play in a game where the group is sharing one paradigm and is really exploring that worldview and its associated myths indepth. Think this covers both genre and focus.<br /> <br /> Scale I'd say mostly local, but it can branch of into global (and better: metaphysical).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T21:35:17-07:00","id":1243397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1239957-interest-recruitment-for-mage-20-pbp?p=1243252#post1243252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm certainly interested. Wether Orphans, Traditions or Technocracy is not of prime interest to me (I can come up with interesting concepts for all of those), but my favourite part about mage is the paradigm (or in M20 terms the Focus, I guess). I'd love to play in a game where the group is sharing one paradigm and is really exploring that worldview and its associated myths indepth. Think this covers both genre and focus.<br /> <br /> Scale I'd say mostly local, but it can branch of into global (and better: metaphysical).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't second this enough. I had plenty of games but very, very few where we actually had something that deep in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T14:38:54-07:00","id":1243606,"title":"","content":"If there's still room for one more player, I'd be really down to join !<br /> <br /> Focus is also the most appealing feature in M20 for me. The idea of playing a mono-Tradition group, but where each player would channel its core paradigm through wildly differents Practices, Tools and Spheres could be awesome. (I've always had a weakness for the Cult of Ecstasy, but any of them could be interesting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as focus, I'd definitely like to see how mundane and mage life intersects. The weird things you can do with the magic system are cool, but I like to see them given context alongside mundane life. I also like to see everyone starting out as newly minted mages. I like the idea of playing a character trying to establish themselves. </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:40:56-07:00","id":1245213,"title":"","content":"Oooh, I missed the sudden flurry of interest. Looks like we have a good start. <br /> <br /> I also find the focus rules to be a huge draw of mage, so I am totally down with exploring paradigm. Let's say we are going to settle on a single tradition then (maybe even a single faction? Or is that a bit narrow?)<br /> <br /> we have one vote for orphans and one for ecstatics (A favourite of mine also, although we would need to discus boundaries and comfort if we went down that road).<br /> <br /> how about genre? Gritty horror?, high magic? Action and adventure? Intrigue? With the focus on paradigm I am guessing we probably want something deeper than an action romp.<br /> <br /> Houlio's suggestion of characters trying to establish themselves sounds like it might be interesting - we could start with newly awakened mages trying to find a place in their new tradition without losing sense of who they were before awakening. Lots of potential to explore their paradigms as they find their place in the world, with how that pans out depending on which tradition they belong to. <br /> <br /> any other preferences? Thoughts on tradition? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T21:28:00-07:00","id":1245320,"title":"","content":"I enjoy mono traditions as well. Action and Adventure is my jam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T23:55:23-07:00","id":1245346,"title":"","content":"Sounds good Damocles. Any preference on which tradition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T00:13:23-07:00","id":1245350,"title":"","content":"Honestly? While my favourite are the Virtual Adepts, I'm partial to the Cult of Ecstasy. It could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T03:12:54-07:00","id":1245379,"title":"","content":"Traditionwise I'm down with most. Seems like the trend is Ecstatics so far, I'm down with that. The only ones I don't really care for are Celestial Chorus and Etherites.<br /> <br /> If we go CoE I think theme wise what we want to focus on is Perception. That's the special thing about them, they perceive the world differently, more intensly. A blurring of the lines between what is real and what is not oh wait it's actually real just not yet err wait I mean it's ephemeral! So basically otherworldly stuff, not just umbral but spatial and temporal distortions, sentient dreams and evolving destinies of quicksilver. I'm not just thinking about a group of people on a mushroom trip here, what I'm trying to express is that the CoE tends to see the world differently, as they are all about sensation and thus where a hermetic sees a mystery as an intellectual problem to solve the cultist feels, experiences he mystery and I think our story should be informed by that.<br /> <br /> That said there's great opportunity to add in action and adventure and/or slice of life to this. And gritty horror... well... there is plenty of potential for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:49:55-07:00","id":1245505,"title":"","content":"We could even have a greater purpose for that. How do we perceive ourselves? Do we have a greater responsibility for having this unique perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:58:38-07:00","id":1245553,"title":"","content":"If perception of self and the world + doubt about the reality of threats around us is meant to be the central theme of the campaign, I'd vouch for at least one or two of the major antagonists to be Marauders. Nothing speaks more about those themes than an Awakened being in constant Quiet, warping reality in his wake, and so far gone in his delusion than the question of his genius or madness is utterly irrelevant.<br /> <br /> As for genre, I'm all for an horror/adventure combination, but I also like to have some kind of intrigue undertone, with the players cultivationg alliances and garnering Influence over different mortal fields of the city, depending on their personal interests and proficiencies (circling back to the them of self-assertion). One of the thematic I really like is the fact that the mages are not simply people with supernatural powers: they're a handful of Awakened in a world that Sleeps, and each of their choices can influence masses without anyone but them being aware of who is really pulling the strings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-13-2018, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T13:05:26-07:00","id":1245611,"title":"","content":"Some great ideas.<br /> <br /> It looks like Ecstatics (or rather the Sahajiya) are the most popular choice. I have to admit I am happy about that. They also seem a great fit for the kind of game and themes we are talking about. Marauders sound like a great thing to explore from an ecstatic perspective. In some respects, they seem like the ecstatic paradigm taken to an extreme with the doors blown wide open but leading to fixation rather than enlightenment. <br /> <br /> I think the next thing we need to consider is location (Spacial and temporal). I tend towards the one mage per 250k people statistic, and like to keep the setting consistent so unless there is a specific reason for mages to gather on mass 'local' needs to either mean a relatively large area or a metropolis of we are going to have enough mages of various traditions to keep things interesting. <br /> <br /> I am not a fan of the revised era where magic was so tight you may as well not have bothered playing mages in the first place, but other than that I am open to suggestions. I like the idea of a modern setting, where revised happened, the traditions were decimated, the masters are gone, but now things are recovering (Ie default M20), but a more retro game with the ascension war still in bloom could also provide an interesting backdrop. <br /> <br /> I am open to suggestions on location;<br /> <br /> England holds a certain draw because it is my home and so I feel it is familiar enough for me to at least try and do it justice, although I think my version of the UK probably differs from official canon somewhat - imwd Britain and the British empire was a success story for the order of reason. It was the birthplace of the industrial revolution, and a stronghold in the ascension war - a place where hermetic and verbena were forced into hiding and religion was subverted as a tool of the state. That changed with the defection of the virtual adepts and the sons of ether. Not only was England the birthplace of industry, but it was also the birthplace of the adepts, and they fought hard here alongside the resurgence of mystical crafts that emerged from hiding. As the ascension war elsewhere was turning against the traditions, in England it raged hotter than ever. Eventually, in the 80s, the union did the unthinkable and withdrew leaving the empty husks of once great industries scattered across the north of the country as Iteration X shifted its focus to the US, and consolidating its hold on the city of London through the syndicate. Their only real influence across the country as a whole comes through the NHS - possibly the progenitors greatest ever success, and so beloved of the sleepers that it operates unchallenged in even the most hard-core of mystical strongholds. Because of the spread out nature of the population (Or maybe just the tiny distances involved compared to somewhere like the states), a campaign here would probably focus on events across several counties - still within an hour or so drive. I doubt the Sahajiya has a huge presence in the isles however (other than through the remnants of helfire clubs...), so you might find yourselves needing to navigate alliances with other traditions.<br /> <br /> Vegas is also appealing, simply because there is a setting book that would help cut down on prep. That said, it does seem to be a decent fit for the themes we are considering.<br /> <br /> It might also be interesting to look at somewhere the Sahajiya is more strongly embedded - exploring the more ancestral paradigms of the Sahajiya alongside more modern interpretations. This would encourage a deeper look at the single tradition and the exotic nature of the location might help throw us outside of our own cultural references an help emphasise the altered perceptions and different ways of looking at things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T14:18:59-07:00","id":1245638,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of playing in the UK. I rand a campaign in Vegas myself at one point, though I ended up using barely anything from the book. That the Sahajiya is not strong in the UK is more of a plus than a negative to me. It means the PCs have more reason to huddle together and opens up lots of plothooks. Afterall if someone needs the touch of an Ecstatic, who else are they going to ask?<br /> <br /> I think a setting where most masters are gone is a good idea, if there was an Avatar Storm I would prefer if it had died down by now though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T22:16:10-07:00","id":1245761,"title":"","content":"I agree with the UK idea. It could look like one of those absolutely awesome and experimental comics from there. Also, please, have the Avatar Storm died down. I liked things the way they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T23:53:19-07:00","id":1245784,"title":"","content":"Agreed about the avatars storm - something that reduced access for mages to do interesting magic never sat well with me. The storm is certainly a thing of the past","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T14:44:15-07:00","id":1246061,"title":"","content":"Right, so it looks like the UK is it.<br /> <br /> I am thinking the Midlands, covering an area roughly corresponding with northern mercia (derby, leistershire, Stafford, and Nottinghamshire mostly, perhaps pushing south as far as Birmingham and north as far as Sheffield). It's a pretty big area in some respects, but depending on the characters we will probably focus on a smaller section of it and it is necessary to have a large enough population to support a decent number of mages.<br /> <br /> So that you can start to think about where you fit in, I see a number of groups having interests in the region:<br /> <br /> Society of Ether:<br /> The industrial revolution was born in rural Derbyshire, and as Iteration x withdrew from the mills and factories the society of ether moved in to fill the vacuum - drawing inspiration from whole industries consigned to history inn a place that was once brimming with inventive energy. Their main British chantry resides at arkwrights mill in Derbyshire where it all started and they maintain several factories, mills, and mines across the area all converted to experiment with forgotten sciences.<br /> <br /> Mercurial Elite:<br /> Bletchley park to the south is somewhat of a mecca for the adepts, but unfortunately it is still in technocratic hands. As a result they are somewhat militant in the British isles, and many still raid the southern technocrat wherever possible before regrouping in the relative safety of the Midlands. <br /> <br /> Order of Hermes:<br /> Before the rise of the order of reason, the hermetic held great strength in Britain and they still maintain several changes and strongholds. The main seat of their power lies further north, but a handful of minor changes dot the region. <br /> <br /> Verbena:<br /> As the technocracies power in Britain dwindled, the verbena emerged from hiding and underwent something of a resurgence. They maintain a number of sacred sites and stone circles across the area.<br /> <br /> Celestial chorus:<br /> The nwo has subverted large parts of the faithful in England to effectively worship the state. Nevertheless, the chorus has regained power to the north, and they maintain a presence in the region.<br /> <br /> Sahajiya:<br /> lastly, and most importantly. A small chantry exists in Nottinghamshire, run by the remnants of a helfire club on the ancestral estates of Lord Byron himself. Depending on your opinion of the code of ananda you may not have much to do with them (at least not by choice) but you probably know of them by reputation if nothing else.<br /> Then there is you. <br /> <br /> if anyone has any ideas they definitely want to see (such as cool ideas for locations on either side of the gauntlet) or definately dont want to see then feel free to throw them into the pot.<br /> <br /> assuming everyone is happy with the location however, let's start to think about characters.<br /> <br /> For each character I need:<br /> <br /> high concept: if they were a film character, how would you describe them?<br /> how do they fit in the sleeping world? Native? Migrant? (From abroad or elsewhere in the uk) job?<br /> how do they fit in the awakened world? Probably overlapping with their high concept.<br /> Paradigm: probably the most interesting part of mage, so let's start thinking about it early. <br /> <br /> You can also start thinking about the mechanical aspects of your character if you wish. We are using the standard character creation rules from mage20 with a couple of exceptions:<br /> <br /> 1) the only ecstatic chantry in the region is the helfire club mentioned (probably a 1 or 2 point chantry) so if you want to belong to a larger chantry it either needs to be that, or be representatives of a more distant chantry (possibly with a portal leading to the region for easy access). Otherwise, if you want a chantry you are going to have to build it yourselves.<br /> 2) Nodes are a commodity that is hard to come by and harder to keep. If you have access to one you need to explain how you gained it, and how you are managing to keep hold of it.<br /> <br /> It is also worth starting to consider links between your characters. Everybody should know at least one other character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T01:47:46-07:00","id":1246215,"title":"","content":"Ok, my character's high concept is a Beautiful Disaster. A character that does whatever she does and to hell with the consequences (This is so going to beplayed for tragedy). Probably a very lonely person and an adrenaline junkie. She latches unto the few people she has and never lets them go.<br /> She lives in the U.K. British-American. The self control of an American and the modesty of a Brit. I 'm sorry for that.<br /> Territorial. Knows about the other Traditions but she feels more at ease in familiar territory.<br /> Her Paradigm is One Way Trip to Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T03:22:32-07:00","id":1246241,"title":"","content":"I'm currently travelling around a bit, so I won't be able to keep up super well here until next week when I return home. I'm personally kinda lukewarm on Ecstatics/Sahajiya, but if we want to do a mono-tradition game I'm more than willing to compromise. It'll just take some more thinking from me to find a concept I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T04:29:10-07:00","id":1246256,"title":"","content":"Looks good damocles.<br /> <br /> Houlio, just catch up where you can. If necessary Im sure we can fit you in as we go. As long as it flies with the others, and you have a character that fits with a group of ecstatics, I dont see a single outsider as necessarily being problematic for a mono tradition game. This especially true for a tradition as open as the Sahajiya. If anything it will provide a different perspective on things and contrast with the ecstatic paradigm everyone else holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T04:48:11-07:00","id":1246257,"title":"","content":"Thanks, although I\u2019ll see what I can do for a Sahajiya too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T02:58:34-07:00","id":1246583,"title":"","content":"My character's concept will be the prodigal son (at least in the contex of the chronicle, all in all he is becoming the wandering sage). He left the UK for a trip to india before starting college and never came back - until now. He spent his years wandering the wild places of the earth, directed only by his gut instinct and sense of curiosity. He learned from many teachers on his way and learned much about the world most city dwellers never will, though his wisdom is more founded in doing and being than in knowing. Now he has decided to return to his roots in the UK and finds his home a foreign world.<br /> <br /> In the sleeping world he is struggling. He doesn't have a job or any money and the thought of confronting his family and erstwhile friend is somewhat daunting. The sheer press of humanity in cities like London feels allmost violently opressive after his time adrift in the wilderness. He's a UK national, but his passport got lost ages ago, so he doesn't have any ID for the moment.<br /> <br /> In he awakened world... he fits everywhere and nowhere. In his travels he studied under many teachers, he studied meditation in a monestary in Khadmandu, trained martial arts with tibetan monks in the himalayas, danced to exhaustion in the deserts surrounded by Djin, drank the strange, hallucigenic juices of various unknown plants in the rainforest and lived with a witch in rural greece for a season. He doesn't know anyone locally, but he probably knows someone who knows someone they know around a few corners and has various teachers and connections to wizards worldwide with affiliations to various traditions and crafts.<br /> <br /> Paradigm: The world is an illusion and only by moving pas thinking can we pierce the veil of deception and discover the true unity of being. This is magic. Unlike many urban Ecstatics he touches upon this tracendent state of mind not through excessive assault of the senses, but through discipline and moderation. Yoga, Tai-Chi and Wushu focus his body and mind, meditation helps him to loose sight of the self and careful deprivation of the senses sensitivizes him to the point where a single kiss or brush of silk against his skin can push his mind from meditative calm to a state more divine.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking he will focus on the Time and Correspondence spheres, piercing the very foundation of the illusion surrounding him. In play I would like to explore learning the mind sphere, which will be quite a journey as I plan on giving him a budding demense wherein he comes into contact with alternative versions of himself that have lived their life differently in some way (he thinks these are time related visions.... and perhaps they are?). He also has the Dream background maxed out, which guided him on his journeys and was one of the reason his many mentors decided to tutor him. Speaking of mentors I also plan on taking high levels of the mentor background to signify a whole slew of mentors of different skill levels ranging of ancient and wise to a kitchen witch he dated for a few months. None of them are local, but they present potential inroads with pretty much any sorcerous society outside the TU and represent a vast reportoire of mystic knowledge.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12226\" data-vbnamecard=\"12226\">Houlio</a> if the CoE is absolutly not to your taste, perhaps look into one of the &quot;adjacent&quot; paradigms. Ahl-I-Batin, Euthanaoi, Akashayana, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 08-16-2018, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T04:58:39-07:00","id":1246601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1239957-interest-recruitment-for-mage-20-pbp?p=1246583#post1246583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12226_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12226\" data-vbnamecard=\"12226\">Houlio</a> if the CoE is absolutly not to your taste, perhaps look into one of the &quot;adjacent&quot; paradigms. Ahl-I-Batin, Euthanaoi, Akashayana, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice! I was actually thinking of making a Euthanatos. I'll have a concept up later tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T05:55:20-07:00","id":1246618,"title":"","content":"Good stuff Flinty.<br /> <br /> So far we have:<br /> <br /> A beautiful disaster riding the wave of adrenaline into oblivion and a wandering sage turned prodigal son using carefully controlled yoga and meditation to open the doors to ecstacy. Looks like some interesting dynamics might develop between those two.<br /> <br /> Do they already know each other (if so how) or are they just about to be thrown together by fate?<br /> <br /> Looking forwards to seeing your concept Houlio.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T06:27:40-07:00","id":1246630,"title":"","content":"Yeah those two probably could learn alot from one another, in their own ways...<br /> <br /> Well I can't speak for damocles but there are a few ways another character could connect to mine that I can think of (and I'm open for other ideas aswell of course):<br /> <br /> My character left the country after finishing school which was a bit under 10 years ago. He's in his mid to late twenties now. Depending on the age of the other characters they could know each other from school (though wether friends, indiffierent or more complicated relationships remains to be determined)<br /> <br /> There could be a familiar connection.<br /> <br /> They could have met him while traveling abroad. He may have not been to cities much, but when it comes to the mystical places of the earth, he's been to many. That reminds me he should definitly hike to stonehenge now that he's in he UK...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:33:19-07:00","id":1246697,"title":"","content":"We could also have been childhood friends. I like that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:43:17-07:00","id":1246699,"title":"","content":"Sure that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T11:12:15-07:00","id":1246706,"title":"","content":"I'm currently hesitating between two concepts. Depending on the Spheres and Abilitie s(and also what you guys think is better), I'll pick either one:<br /> <br /> A) <b>Harold Alderson</b>, a hypnotherapist during the day, and active member of the local gay leather during the night. His Awakening took place during an underground rave, as he stumbled upon a Bahari ritual: the breakthrough led to his conversion, making him what a Cainite would call a Lilin Witch - not particularly tied to the Cult of Lilith, but sharing its tenets and its faith. He joined the Sahajiya because of their acceptance for passion and disinhibition, but struggles to reconcile the code of Ananda (everyone's free will and integrity in the research of their passion should be respected) with his Ba'ham creed (transformative pain is to be endured and inflicted - and even forced, when someone doesn't accept it).<br /> <br /> Probably has the Cyclic Magick Merit/Flaw (his Magick strengthening as the night advances, reaching its climax at midnight and then decreasing and reaching a low at noon).<br /> <br /> <b>Mundane Activities</b>: Harold has the ear and trust of many a rich man, be them his daily patients or his nightly lovers. He uses those connections to bring weight to his subtle but constant activism for the LGBT community.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakened Activities</b>: As one of the rare Awakened, non-affiliated to the NHS therapists in town, Harold is a popular choice for magi who try to cope with the mental burdens brought by their powers. Also, as an enthusiast organizer of Ecstatic group rites (with the occasional inclusion of fragments of Bahari lore), he often oversees other Traditions' ritual celebrations, incorporating.<br /> <br /> <b>Focus: </b>In all but in name, Harold is a Ba\u2019ham. His beliefs about adaptation and learning through suffering find their expression in the Spheres of Life, Mind and Prime, canalyzed through the trappings of BDSM and the Bacchanalian undertones he learned in the Hellfire Club. However, more than physical pain, Harold\u2019s magick revolves more about bliss, trust and letting go.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm</b>: <i>A</i> <i>World of Gods and Monsters, Transcend All Your Limits</i><br /> <b>Practices</b>: Dominion, Art of Desire, Witchcraft<br /> <b>Instruments</b>: Knots and Ropes, Social Domination, Eye Contact, Fashion (leather gear), Transgression, Group Rites, Bodywork.<br /> <b>Personalized Instrument (Life)</b>: Consensual sexual activities.<br /> <b>Unique Instrument</b>: ?<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> B) <b>Lyss</b>, a drug dealer (although she prefers to be refered as either a &quot;narco-alchemist&quot; or a &quot;entheogenic sommelier&quot;.) , she has earned street cred amongst Awakened and regular mortals alike for her ability to always propose the adequate substance for each of her customers: when it's not enough, she resorts to her Spheres of predilection (Life and Matter, plus either Mind or Spirits) to create vivid hallucination.<br /> <br /> She's probably Prone to Quiet, and possibly has the Cyclic Magick Merit/Flaw (same as Harold, climax at midnight and low at noon).<br /> Probably has the Demesne and/or the Totem Background.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm</b>: <i>Consciousness is the Only True Reality. </i>Therefore, using drugs means <i>Turning Keys to Reality. </i>The disinhibition brought by drugs will allow us to <i>Transcend All Our Limits</i>.In our era, drugs are more potent and widespread than ever: we should <i>Embrace the Threshold </i>and roll with it!<br /> <br /> <b>Practices</b>: Alchemy, Art of Desire, Crazy Wisdom<br /> <b>Instruments</b>: Brews and Powders, Drugs and Poisons, Crossroads and Crossing Times, Voice (Rhymes), Inscriptions, Cups and vessels, Laboratory.<br /> <br /> Personalized Instrument: Cups and vessels. Unique Instrument: A syringe?<br /> <br /> <br /> NB: I'm using elements from the M20 Book of Secrets to build my character. If it isn't allowed, please tell me, and I'll rework it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-16-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T18:39:41-07:00","id":1247257,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's what I have come up with:<br /> <br /> <b>High Concept:</b> &quot;The brightest star burns out twice as fast&quot;, my character was a really promising student in both his awakened and sleeper life, but he's recently lost most of his motivation to continue on the path laid out for him. His relationships with teachers are fraying, and he's in the process of trying to figure out what he wants his life to be.<br /> <b>Sleeping World:</b> My character is a graduate student at Oxbridge, but he never really fit easily into any on discipline. He straddles the line a lot between philosophy, biology, and writing. He knows a lot of the faculty and a wide swath of other graduate students, but his recent decision to move out into the Midlands &quot;to work on his dissertation away from distractions&quot; has distanced him from most of them. He is still getting his fellowship, but unless he actually starts producing some work, he is likely to get cut from the program.<br /> <b>Awakened World:</b> After he awakened, he was picked up by an esteemed Euthanatos for training and initiation. For a few months, everything was great, but my character recently started to see the world in a pretty different light to his mentor. Their relationship has begun to deteriorate as he and his mentor have a rather fundamental disagreement about the nature of reality and magic. He believes moving away with a group of ecstatics to get some real magic done will help him figure out his own ideas and beliefs outside of the constraining influence of his mentor. I imagine he's from the UK as well.<br /> <b>Paradigm</b><b>:</b> My character definitely believes in <i>Heavenly Order and Earthly Chaos</i>, specifically that there is some sort of ideal plan for how everything ought to pass from one state to another. However, humans have mucked it all up so that the world as it exists today is a kind of unnatural abomination. <br /> <br /> As far as mechanics goes, I imagine him focusing a lot on entropy and life. I'll pick a number of merits to reflect his one Euthanatoi mentor as well as his connections back to his graduate institution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T23:21:39-07:00","id":1247292,"title":"","content":"Looks really good.<br /> <br /> The next important thing is figuring out if you guys already know each other. If so, how?<br /> <br /> If you do know each other then are you operating as a cabal already? If you are then do you potentially have any shared resources (sanctum / node etc)?<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I think we just need to get the mechanical side of the characters written up and we can get started.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T02:01:29-07:00","id":1247310,"title":"","content":"I'd like to do an &quot;origin story&quot;. Sort of. Like, we should start with our meeting and forming a Cabal. Also, I'm getting right trough my sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T04:00:20-07:00","id":1247332,"title":"","content":"I'm open to having previous ties to the other players in some form, but since my character has only recently returned I don't think he is a member of the cabal allready. Even if he knows the other PCs from &quot;before&quot; it's likely that he has no clue they are awakened unless they met on the road somewhere in the last few years.<br /> <br /> My sheet is more or less done, I'm just weighing a few merits and flaws against each other, examining them for plothook potential etc.<br /> <br /> May I ask what form the actual game will take? pbp, but where? Here, discord, roll20, somewhere else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T10:32:52-07:00","id":1247425,"title":"","content":"My sheet is basically done, I'll post it tomorrow. I believe we are doing this PbP and here. I'm ok with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T11:11:09-07:00","id":1247437,"title":"","content":"It'll be a couple days before I can get my sheet up. I kinda like the idea of doing an origin story, or at least making sure everyone is linked to one or two other people or something. I wouldn't say having a &quot;link&quot; needs to be &quot;I've known you for years&quot;, but it needs to be a reason to willingly work with the other person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T11:23:28-07:00","id":1247439,"title":"","content":"A common enemy? Or a destiny? And I'm not saying this because I may have put a few background points of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T04:37:28-07:00","id":1247664,"title":"","content":"PbP. Probably in the PbP forum here, but if anyone knows a forum that is better set up to facilitate it then I would be happy to migrate (forums that have inbuilt dice rollers are a godsend, but it is easy enough to just link orokos or something).<br /> <br /> Meeting for an origin story is not a problem. Finding an excuse to get you all in the same place with a crisis to deal with is easy enough, as is finding some common ground to bind you together. Forming and building a cabal, carving out your own niche in the world, might be quite an interesting journey.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T09:32:02-07:00","id":1247739,"title":"","content":"Alright, here it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Paulette &quot;Polly&quot; Kinley<br /> <b>Affilations</b><b>:</b> Traditions<br /> <b>Sect:</b> Cult of Ecstasy<br /> <b>Nature</b>: Survivor<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Rogue<br /> <b>Essence: </b>Questing<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Beautiful Disaster<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:<br /> Strenght:</b>2<br /> <b>Dexterity:</b>4<br /> <b>Stamina:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma: </b>4<br /> <b>Manipulation:</b>3<br /> <b>Appearance:</b>3<br /> <br /> <b>Perception: </b>2<br /> <b>Intelligence:</b>1<br /> <b>Wits:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:<br /> Alertness:</b>2<br /> <b>Art (Dance):</b>2<br /> <b>Athletics:</b>1<br /> <b>Brawl:</b> 2<br /> <b>Empathy (Hidden Feelings) :</b>3<br /> <b>Intimidation:</b> 2<br /> <b>Streetwise (Drug Trade):</b>1<br /> <b>Subterfuge:</b>2<br /> <br /> <b>Drive: </b>2<br /> <b>Etiquette:</b>1<br /> <b>Firearms: </b>1<br /> <b>Meditation:</b>1<br /> <b>Stealth:</b>2<br /> <b>Technology:</b>2<br /> <br /> <b>Computer:</b> 1<br /> <b>Esoterica:</b>1<br /> <b>Investigation:</b>2<br /> <b>Occult:</b>2<br /> <br /> <b>Spheres:<br /> Entropy:</b>1<br /> <b>Forces:</b>2<br /> <b>Prime:</b>1<br /> <b>Time</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b><br /> <b>Avatar: </b>2<br /> <b>Back Up (Gangsters &amp; Vigilantes):</b>2<br /> <b>Chantry:</b>1<br /> <b>Contacts:</b>1<br /> <b>Destiny:</b>3<br /> <b>Resources:</b>1<br /> <br /> <b>Arete:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 5<br /> <b>Merits &amp; Flaws:</b> Derangement (BPD)<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm</b>: <i>Everything is Chaos, One Way Trip to Oblivion</i><br /> <b>Practices</b>: Art of Desire, Chaos Magick, Witchcraft<br /> <b>Instruments</b>: Dances and Movement, Drus and Poisons, Energy, Sex and Sensuality, Social Domination, Symbols, Tricks &amp; Illusions<br /> <br /> If you look at the voice &quot;Problem Child&quot;, you'll find Polly's photo, address, social security number and a small biography. The shrinks thought she had something &quot;not right&quot;. Her parents were the first to agree. What Polly had was far more complicated than that: She craved attention and love and had no one that gave it to her. That's why she decided to go around and mingle with very bad people. People that did bad things but thought she was fun. That's everything she needed. That was until she Awakened. One of her &quot;normal&quot; friends, the one person she didn't want to involve in her messes did get involved. And lo and behold, when everything seemed lost...She turned back time.Like it never happened. She stopped her from ever getting out of her home and in that mess. No one knows about it. Normal people would think she's crazy. Fortunately, she doesn't see that much normal people around. She found herself an abandoned place for her to practice and now? Now she has to find her place in a bigger world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","user":"damocles23","date":". 08-21-2018, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T01:05:53-07:00","id":1247941,"title":"","content":"<b><b>Name</b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Arunah Dewan</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Primordial<br /> <b>Nature: </b>Hacker<br /> <b>Demeanor: </b>Romantic<br /> <b>Tradition</b>: Sahajjiya<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Modern Courtesan<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Intelligence 4, Wits 2, Resolve 2<br /> <br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Manipulation 4, Charisma 4, Appearance 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Strength 1<br /> <i>A slender body, just not meager enough to be totally morbid. Mostly indifferent (and vaguely distasted by) her fleshly shell: her grace and speed are mostly due to her iron-grip on her senses, and her stamina to her ability to overlook physical inconveniences. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Knowledges</b>: Pharmacopeia 3, Area Knowledge 1, Enigma 1, Cosmology 1 (Umbral Protocols)<br /> <b>Talents</b>: Athletics 1, Subterfuge 2, Carousing 2 (Overcoming Inhibitions), Art (Mandala) 2, Seduction 2, Empathy 1, Awareness 2, Expression 1<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Stealth 1, Research 1, Etiquette 2<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Arcane 2, Avatar 1,Chantry 1, Library 1, Patron 1, Spies 2<br /> <br /> <b>Arete</b>: 3<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 5<br /> <b>Spheres</b>: Life 3 (affinity sphere), Spirits 2, Matter 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Enchanting Features (Merit 2 pts) </b>(BoS p.37): Her eyes.<br /> <br /> 15 Freebie Points - 8 (Arete 3) = 7<br /> - 7 (+1 Sphere Dot) = 0<br /> +4 (Prone to Quiet) = 4<br /> -2 (Enchanting Features) = 2<br /> -1 (Arcane Background) = 1<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prone to Quiet (Flaw 4 pts) </b>(BoS p.91): The Colors are pretty. The Colors are endless in their nuances and gradients. The Colors are maddeningly beautiful \u2013 and when they find a crack in Lyss\u2019 mind, they more than happily slip through it and begin to paint unreal tableaux in the back of her head. The Colors are insane \u2013 and Lyss, often, gets insane too. <i>Quiet is her default Paradox backlash, and so a backlash of five points or more automatically sends her into Quiet.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cyclical Magic (Merit/Flaw 3pts)</b> (BoS p.70): The Black of night is the perfect canvas for Lyss\u2019 compositions, as it contains all colors in potentiality: to the contrary, the white of daylight is a blank slate that erodes her Color arrangements.<br /> <br /> <u>Night</u><br /> 22h00 to 23h00: -1 difficulty to spellcasting.<br /> 23h00 to 00h00: -2 difficulty.<br /> 00h00 to 01h00: -3 difficulty<br /> 01h00 to 02h00: -2 difficulty.<br /> 04h00 to 06h00: -1 difficulty.<br /> 06h00 to 10h00: no effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Day</u><br /> 10h00 to 11h00: +1 difficulty to spellcasting.<br /> 11h to 12h00: +2 difficulty.<br /> 12h00 to 13h00: +3 difficulty.<br /> 13h00 to 14h00: +2 difficulty.<br /> 14h00 to 15h00: +1 difficulty.<br /> and 15h00 to 22h00: no effect.<br /> <br /> &lt;Biography In Progress&gt;<br /> <br /> <b><u>Focus: Colors from Outer Space</u></b><br /> When it comes to Focus, Arunah adamantly refuse to give any kind of prominence to her Hindi legacy \u2013 or, for that matters, to any traditions. She\u2019s eclectic and syncretic, absorbing all kinds of influences and simply subordinating them to the core tenet of her paradigm. Magic, she affirms, derives from the Seven Colors from which the Canvas of the universe is composed: seven Colors so far off the spectrum as we know it that no sane human could hope to ever perceive \u2013 or even conceive \u2013 them. Only when in the throes of Passion (those that most humans deem on the verge of madness), can the soul perceive a glimmer of the Seven Glorious Shades: <a href=\"http://thefifthcity.wikia.com/wiki/The_Neathbow\" target=\"_blank\">Irrigo, Violant, Cosmogone, Peligin, Apocyan, Viric and Gant.</a> In normal times, those Colors are asleep within the Maya (the Tapestry), disseminated through the Spheres: the visible colors, especially when they\u2019re all gathered in the form of daylight, obscuring them. An Awakened is simply someone who can perceive those colors and scrape the patina of the world, liberating them, and recasting them in a way that makes him, if only for a time, a demiurgic Painter of the Cosmos.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm</b>: Aliens Made Us What We Are, All the World\u2019s A Stage, Turning the Keys to Reality<br /> <br /> <b>Practices</b>: Crazy Wisdom, plus some rudiments of spiritualism closer to Voodoo than to Shamanism.<br /> <br /> <b>Instruments</b>: Powders and pigments, Drugs and Poisons, Crossroads and Crossing Times, Group Rites, Circles and Pentacles, Artworks, Eye Contact.<br /> <br /> <b>Personalized Instrument</b>: Eye Contact. Arunah's irises swirl with colors impossible, and anyone gazing back at them risks to have the colors of his own Pattern animated and blurred by those twin maelstroms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 08-20-2018, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T13:45:57-07:00","id":1248202,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3997\" data-vbnamecard=\"3997\">damocles23</a> I think something's wrong with your char's stats. You've got 6/4/3 attributes spent instead of 7/5/3.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Boxcar Jones, the magic hobo<br /> <br /> .... just kidding.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Leeland &quot;Lee&quot; Jones<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Visionary<br /> <b>Demeanor: </b>Kid<br /> <b>Essence:</b> Questing<br /> <b>Tradition</b>: Sahajjiya - sort of kinda. He's learned from a lot of people and never officially joined some kind of global magic organization... but that's what some people called him and he's cool with that<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Prodigal Son<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes</b>: Perception 5 (Attuned), Intelligence 3, Wits 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes</b>: Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Physical Attributes</b>: Strength 1, Dexterity 4 (Quick), Stamina 3<br /> <br /> <b>Talents</b>: Alertness 3, Athletics 2, Awareness 3, Empathy 3, Leadership 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Martial Arts 3, Meditation 3, Survival 3<br /> <b>Knowledges</b>: Cosmology 1, Enigmas 3, Occult 1<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> <b>Avatar</b>: 2 - His avatar appears to him as different versions of himself, sometimes past or future, sometimes contemporary but whose history is somehow different. It mostly appears to him within his demense<br /> <b>Demense:</b> 1 - When he dreams (or is in very deep Meditation) he finds himself in places he's been before, but slightly different. He thinks his consciousness is superceeding the illusion and touching upon others, dreaming of alternate universes or timelines.<br /> <b>Dream:</b> 5 - He's allways had a special, subconcious connection to the human overmind, the akashic record, whatever you want to call it. At times he exhibits strange, but profound insights and this is one of the reasons many of his teachers agreed to train him<br /> <b>Mentor:</b> 5 - Like some sailors are said to have a wife in every port, Lee seems to find teachers willing to share their knowledge with him wherever he goes. This reaches from mundane humans, to thaumaturges, to mages not much more powerful himself to some reclusive and terrifying masters of earth shattering power. They're scattered all over the world and their relationship to lee vastly depends on the mentor in question. He's learned secret tantric rites from the legendary vratja, studied the secrets of space and connection under a mysterious sufi in Afghanistan, practiced Martial Arts in a tibetan monastery and so on and so forth. On the upside this gives him a vast array of knowledge he can aquire by asking the right person and an in with most traditions as he invariably knows the mentor of a friend of a friend. On the downside none of them are local to GB (and barely any call europe their home).<br /> <br /> <b>Arete</b>: 3<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 8<br /> <b>Spheres</b>: Correspondence 3, Time (Affinity Sphere) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> Concentration (BoS p. 43), Natural Linguist (BoS p. 45), Languages (M20 p. 643) Hindi and Arabic<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws:</b><br /> <b>Curious (BoS p. 48)</b><br /> <b>Blacklisted (BoS p. 59)</b> - 1 While not blacklisted per se Lee has no valid indentification and has during his long absence (nearly a decade!) been legally declared dead<br /> <b>Family Issues (BoS p. 62)</b> - 1 Reuniting with his family will be hard as he's been missing for years. His sister took his absence especially badly and has (partly because of it) developed a drug abuse problem, though Lee does not know about that yet<br /> <b>Infamy (BoS p. 62)</b> - 1 Lee just returned to the UK from a prolonged stint in the mountains of rural Afghanistan. He looks like a barefoot hobo and will likely have trouble adjusting to city (even &quot;country&quot;) live in a civilized country, facing stigmata along the way until he &quot;cleans his act up&quot;<br /> <b>Strangeness (BoS p. 85)</b> - Time and Space itself become malleable around Lee, even without his active meddling<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm:</b> Everything is an Illusion<br /> <b>Practices</b>: Tantra, Yoga and a good dash of Crazy Wisdom<br /> <b>Instruments</b>: Bodywork, Dances, Gestures, Postures and Other Movement Practices, Drugs and Poisons, Energy, Eye Contact, Martial Arts, Meditation, Ordeals and Exertion, Sex and Sensuality, Sympathy<br /> <br /> His practice of magic is rather eclectic, but ultimately all result in transcending the concious state of being for a more sublime form of awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T20:59:50-07:00","id":1248296,"title":"","content":"I'll be back to regular internet connection this evening, and I'll have time to post up my sheet then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T21:56:05-07:00","id":1248317,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a>, I fixed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T21:03:23-07:00","id":1250161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1239957-interest-recruitment-for-mage-20-pbp#post1239957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(actually I would be willing to start out with up to 6, to cover the inevitable attrition with play by post games, but I would be reluctant to start with less than 3)</div> </div> </div> </div>My wife and I are desperate for a M20 game- if you have openings in the future and would like to include other traditions in your story, feel free to message me. I check into OPP Forums every once in a while, but if you're immediately looking for new players, you can find us on our pbp forum's discord server: <a href=\"https://discord.gg/dvEH3er\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/dvEH3er</a><br /> <br /> Good luck <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14453\" data-vbnamecard=\"14453\">Tamuz</a> ! I feel like pbp Mage STs are the chosen one every time I see one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i43.photobucket.com/albums/e384/GrottyGilgamesh/3812c9a0-1510-4235-a3d4-1993f1a47b4b_zpsd6723580.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":4266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4266-mousegbn","user":"MouseGBN","date":". 08-31-2018, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4266-mousegbn","name":"MouseGBN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4266_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}